  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Friday)\nIssued at 125 PM MDT Sat Oct 3 2026\n\nThe H5 ridge will weaken Monday while drifting southeast into NM \nahead of an H5 shortwave trough entering the Great Basin. A 50-60kt \nspeed max in association with this trough will slide southeast from \nnorthern AZ Monday then into western NM Tuesday and southern NM by \nWednesday. Greater mid level moisture and lift with the upper level \nshortwave trough will increase the chance for showers and storms \nover the northern and western high terrain Monday thru Wednesday. \n12Z models have trended toward slightly greater coverage but chances \nare still very low. Max temps will remain within +/-5F of normal \nwith light winds outside of any showers.\n\nExtended forecast guidance is still in good agreement building a \nweak shortwave ridge eastward into NM Thursday and Friday in the \nwake of the departing upper low near the Big Bend region. Temps will \nstay near normal in this pattern with light winds Thursday becoming \na tad more breezy for eastern NM by Friday.",
